Kept bespoke
============

Two files stay hand-written, because what they check is not a workload
with an invariant:

  900_serializable.pl   The gapless-sequence and write-skew SSI tests.
                        Their whole point is a table with no unique
                        constraint and a very specific transaction shape;
                        expressing that as a load plus a check would
                        weaken it.

  901_pg_dump.pl        Dump and restore is an external process, not a
                        pgbench script, and its invariant is a
                        comparison between two databases.

Both pick up the Layer 0 helpers (seeding, backtraces, the REPACK
tolerance) but keep their own structure.

Gaps this rewrite has not closed
================================

These were covered by the old files and are not covered to the same
depth yet.  They are listed rather than quietly dropped, because the old
files are gone from the tree and only the git history has them:

  logical replication depth   The 'subscription' environment runs the
                              publisher's workload and checks that the
                              subscriber ends up with the same data,
                              which is what 007 did.  What is missing is
                              022's local write contention on the very
                              rows being applied, 023's repeated initial
                              table synchronization, and 010's DDL on
                              the subscriber side.  Each needs a load
                              that runs against the subscriber rather
                              than the publisher, which the environment
                              does not offer yet.

  cross-database decoding     027 ran REPACK churn in one database while
                              a slot decoded another.  Needs a load
                              targeting a second database.

  xid-assigning index         029 built indexes whose expressions
  expressions                 acquire a transaction id, which changes
                              how the build's phases interact with
                              snapshots and horizons.

  session_replication_role    031 drove a workload in replica mode
                              against a table with RLS and replica-mode
                              triggers.

  REPACK's MVCC tolerance     Only the 'balances' check tolerates a
                              relation reading empty across a
                              relfilenode swap.  The other checks assume
                              they will not span one, which is true at
                              the rate the rotation currently runs but
                              is not guaranteed.
